From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kamil=20Postro=C5=BCny?= <kamil@postrozny.pl>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:09:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: release a WoW64 window before the exiting process's
 socket closes

process_exit_wrapper closed a child pseudo-process's master socket and
only then, in ios_jit_reclaim_process, released its WoW64 window. The
window's teardown makes server calls; with the socket closed the server
had already killed the thread, so the first of them aborted it while it
held ios_wow64_windows_lock, which is not an uninterrupted section and
so is not given back at abort. Every other process's next
NtQueryVirtualMemory then waited on that lock for ever. House of Golf 2's
prerequisite installer (WiX Burn) hung this way when the VC++
redistributable's elevated child exited: its parent stopped in
ios_wow64_route_query, holding the FEX lock, and the chain never ended.

Release the window where the fixed-base main image is retired, before
the socket closes. The later call in ios_jit_reclaim_process then finds
the window gone, or retired while secondary threads remain, and does
nothing.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-uepre-authenticode.md
Offered-upstream: no; owner-local WoW64 VM is Playport code
---
 build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c  |  6 ++++++
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
index eaa243d..dcd1d4f 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
@@ -3971,6 +3971,12 @@ void process_exit_wrapper( int status )
          * NtUnmapViewOfSection needs a live server connection, and this is the
          * last moment we have one while still on the owning process's thread. */
         ios_retire_own_fixed_base_image( dead_peb );
+        /* Playport: the WoW64 window too, for the same reason: its teardown
+         * makes server calls (virtual_ios.c ios_wow64_release_window_at_exit). */
+        {
+            extern void ios_wow64_release_window_at_exit( void *owner );
+            ios_wow64_release_window_at_exit( dead_peb );
+        }
         ios_fdt_note_close( ios_proc_sockets[i].fd, "exit-master", dead_peb );
         close( ios_proc_sockets[i].fd );
         ios_proc_sockets[i].peb = NULL;
diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 1e99477..af79319 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -16059,6 +16059,18 @@ static void ios_wow64_release_window( void *owner )
     pthread_mutex_unlock( &ios_wow64_windows_lock );
 }
 
+/* process_exit_wrapper's call, while the exiting process still has its server
+ * connection: the teardown makes server calls, and once the master socket is
+ * closed the server kills this thread in the first of them. It then ended
+ * holding ios_wow64_windows_lock, and every other process's next
+ * NtQueryVirtualMemory waited for it for ever (a WiX Burn chain whose child
+ * exited never saw it end). ios_jit_reclaim_process's later call then finds
+ * the window gone or retired and does nothing. */
+void ios_wow64_release_window_at_exit( void *owner )
+{
+    ios_wow64_release_window( owner );
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_map_main_module
  */
